1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:10,500
Before creation began... Sree Maha Vishu rested upon Ananta. Whenever dharma fades... He descends.

2
00:00:12,600 --> 00:00:19,300
In the great deluge... Matsya guided the sacred ark, preserving the eternal Vedas.

3
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:28,500
As the cosmic ocean was churned... the Divine Tortoise, Kurma, bore Mount Mandara upon His back to steady creation.

4
00:00:30,600 --> 00:00:38,500
Plunging into the dark abyss... the Divine Boar, Varaha, lifted Mother Earth upon His sacred tusks, restoring Her to light.

5
00:00:40,600 --> 00:00:48,500
Bursting forth from the shattered pillar... the fierce Man-Lion, Narasimha, destroyed arrogance and protected unwavering devotion.

6
00:00:50,600 --> 00:00:58,500
Measuring the universe in three strides... the Divine Youth, Vamana, revealed that true humility surpasses all earthly power.

7
00:01:00,600 --> 00:01:08,600
Wielding the battle-axe of righteousness... Parashurama punished corrupt tyranny and decreed power must serve dharma.

8
00:01:10,600 --> 00:01:18,600
Mariyada Purushottama... Sri Rama sacrificed everything, proving that truth and righteousness must triumph.

9
00:01:20,600 --> 00:01:28,600
Upon the battlefield of Kurukshetra... Bhagavan Sri Krishna unveiled the Bhagavad Gita, the immortal light of wisdom.

10
00:01:30,600 --> 00:01:38,600
Forsaking the illusions of power... Gautama Buddha illuminated the path of inner peace, boundless compassion, and truth.

11
00:01:40,600 --> 00:01:48,600
Riding the blazing white steed Devadatta... the final avatara, Kalki, descends to conquer darkness and herald the golden age.

12
00:01:50,600 --> 00:02:00,000
Across cosmic time... Sree Maha Vishu protects the universe. Dharma will rise again. Om Namo Narayanaya.

